# Pull-out of a centrically embedded rebar from a concrete cylinder.
# Node generator input (T3D-free qhull pipeline).
#
# Specimen: cylinder length 100 mm (axis along x), diameter 100 mm (R = 50 mm).
# Rebar:    diameter 16 mm (R = 8 mm), centric, with a 0.1 mm interface (ITZ)
#           shell that carries the steel<->concrete bond contact elements.
# Coarse mesh (diam = 10 mm) because the specimen is long; the interface is
# refined so the bond shell is resolved around the bar circumference.
#@output nodes.dat
#@domain 3
#@diam 1.0e-2
#@maxiter 100000
#@ranint -2
#@perflag 3 0 0 0
#@ranflag 1
# bounding-box corners widen the localiser beyond the cylinder region
#@vertex 1 coords 3 -0.01 -0.055 -0.055
#@vertex 2 coords 3  0.11  0.055  0.055
#@cylinder 1 line 6 0. 0. 0. 0.1 0. 0. radius 0.05 refine 1.0
#@interfacecylinder 1 line 6 0. 0. 0. 0.1 0. 0. radius 0.008 refine 0.5 itz 0.1e-3
